# Desert at night.
#
# A map of the game (SceneStage, "Desierto de noche" in the Z debug
# selector) and what the web viewer (tools/scene_viewer/) shows. Format: one command per line, fields separated by
# spaces, '#' starts a comment. Model paths are relative to assets/.
# Full reference: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, section "Ficheros de escena".

# Direction towards the moon (normalised on load). Must match MOON_DIR in
# assets/sky/generate_sky.py, the moon is painted into the sky texture.
moon    -0.32 0.26 -0.91
# Moonlight colour (r g b), cool and dim
light   0.28 0.34 0.62
# Horizon colour: clear colour and fog colour
fog     0.035 0.055 0.110

# Sky dome, always centred on the camera and drawn without depth
sky     sky/skydome.obj

# The player (a Walker): model x y z. "ground" as y stands it on the floor
player  ping/PenguinoAnimado.fbx  0 ground 0
# Camera: distance behind the player, height above its feet. Distance 0 is
# first person (the player is not drawn); 1.6 is the penguin's eye level.
camera  0 1.6

# What the player walks on (and the height that "ground" refers to):
# floor <model> <x> <y> <z>
floor   desert/dunes.obj  0 -1 0

# object <model> <x> <y> <z> <yaw (rad)> <scale> [lit|emissive|breathe]
#
# y is a world height, or "ground": on the floor at (x, z), sunk 0.05 so
# nothing floats on the slopes (SceneStage::PROP_SINK). The dunes are
# regenerated now and then (assets/desert/generate_assets.py), so props
# use "ground" rather than fixed heights.

object  desert/cactus_a.obj    -4.5  ground     -8   0.5    1
object  desert/cactus_a.obj       8   ground    -16     2  1.3
object  desert/cactus_a.obj     -16   ground    -24     4  1.6
object  desert/cactus_a.obj      18   ground    -30     1  1.2
object  desert/cactus_b.obj     5.5  ground    -10     3  1.1
object  desert/cactus_b.obj      -9   ground    -14   5.5  1.2
object  desert/cactus_b.obj      14   ground    -22   0.8  1.5
object  desert/rock_a.obj        -4  ground     -6   0.3    1
object  desert/rock_a.obj        11   ground     -9   2.5  1.8
object  desert/rock_a.obj       -20   ground    -12   4.5  2.5
object  desert/rock_b.obj       3.5  ground   -4.5   1.2    1
object  desert/rock_b.obj        -8  ground    -11   3.3  1.4
object  desert/rock_b.obj         7   ground    -18     5  1.7
object  desert/rock_b.obj        -3   ground    -14   0.1  1.1

# The creature, standing in the distance and facing the camera. It breathes
# (vertex shader) and its eyes glow (emissive, no lighting or fog).
object  creature/creature.obj       1.5  ground  -13  0.25  1  breathe
object  creature/creature_eyes.obj  1.5  ground  -13  0.25  1  emissive
